## Commands

- Check: `bin/check` (lint, shell syntax, whitespace, tests). Run it before you call work done.
- Behavior proof comes from a project run skill. In Claude Code, ask the user to type `/run-skill-generator` (manual-only) to create one, with a doctor step and an evidence folder; where pstack is installed, ask for `/pstack:create-verification-skill` instead, which names it `verify-<project>`.
- Proof runs on the real target. A step run on a stand-in stays marked unverified until it runs there.

